  "problem": {
    "statement": "JIRA Issue: DOC-3188\n\nTitle: Member Roles Developer Docs and Auth Pages Update\n\nDescription:\n## Problem\n\nXperience by Kentico v31.3.0 introduces member roles via [ASP.NET](http://ASP.NET) Core Identity. The existing registration-and-authentication pages explicitly state \"Xperience does not support roles\" and use the now-deprecated `NoOpApplicationRole`/`NoOpApplicationRoleStore`. There is also no documentation for the role-specific APIs: programmatic role management, role assignment, extending `ApplicationRole`, custom authorization patterns.\n\nThis task covers both:\n\n  * **Creating** a new member roles subpage with role-specific developer scenarios\n  * **Updating** existing auth pages to enable roles and remove deprecated NoOp types\n\n## Description\n\n### Part A — New Member Roles Page\n\nCreate a new documentation page under registration-and-authentication focused on member role management and customization:\n\n  1. **Programmatic role management** — CRUD via `ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>` (Identity level) AND via `IInfoProvider<MemberRoleInfo>` (ObjectQuery level), clearly separated by use case\n  2. **Role assignment/unassignment** — `ApplicationUserStore<ApplicationUser>.AddToRoleAsync()`, `RemoveFromRoleAsync()`, `GetRolesAsync()`, `IsInRoleAsync()`\n  3. **Extend **`ApplicationRole` — Custom properties via `MapFromMemberRoleInfo()` / `MapToMemberRoleInfo()` (mirrors existing `ApplicationUser` customization pattern in `add-fields-to-member-objects.md`)\n  4. **Custom authorization at the business layer** — Best practice: no extension points in the Xperience security pipeline; custom auth must run after content retrieval\n  5. `[Authorize]` attribute support — Brief note that standard [ASP.NET](http://ASP.NET) `[Authorize(Roles = \"RoleName\")]` works for member roles since they are Identity roles with claims (cross-link to existing `secure-custom-endpoints.md` for admin endpoint authorization)\n  6. **Admin preview behavior** — Brief note: all role-restricted content is visible in preview/page builder (dummy identity with all roles)\n\n### Part B — Auth Pages: Enable Roles + NoOp Deprecation\n\nRewrite all code samples and descriptive text in the registration-and-authentication section to use the new `ApplicationRole`/`ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>` types. This is where \"how to enable roles\" is documented.\n\n#### 1. `registration-and-authentication.md` (parent page)\n\n  * **REMOVE**: \"NoOpApplicationRole and NoOpApplicationRoleStore – Xperience **does not support** roles and role management...\"\n  * **REPLACE WITH**: Description of `ApplicationRole` and `ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>` as the Identity role implementation, with link to new member roles subpage\n  * **UPDATE**: Code sample — `AddIdentity<ApplicationUser, NoOpApplicationRole>` → `AddIdentity<ApplicationUser, ApplicationRole>` with full registration including `ApplicationRoleStore` and `RoleManager`\n  * **ADD**: Brief explanation that enabling roles requires registering `ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>` and `RoleManager<ApplicationRole>` in the Identity pipeline\n\n#### 2. `forms-authentication.md`\n\n  * **UPDATE**: All code samples — `NoOpApplicationRole` → `ApplicationRole`, full service registration with real role types\n\n#### 3. `external-authentication.md`\n\n  * **UPDATE**: Code sample — `NoOpApplicationRole` → `ApplicationRole`, `NoOpApplicationRoleStore` → `ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>`\n\n#### 4. `add-fields-to-member-objects.md`\n\n  * **UPDATE**: Code sample — `ExtendedApplicationUser, NoOpApplicationRole` → `ExtendedApplicationUser, ApplicationRole`\n  * **ADD**: Brief note about the parallel pattern for extending `ApplicationRole`, linking to the new member roles page\n\n## Affected Files\n\n### Documentation\n\n|Action|File Path|Details|\n|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n|CREATE |`src/_documentation/_documentation/developers-and-admins/development/registration-and-authentication/member-roles.md` |New page: role CRUD, assignment, customization, [Authorize], custom auth patterns |\n|UPDATE |`src/_documentation/_documentation/developers-and-admins/development/registration-and-authentication.md` |Remove \"not supported\" statement, rewrite code samples, add role enablement |\n|UPDATE |`src/_documentation/_documentation/developers-and-admins/development/registration-and-authentication/forms-authentication.md` |Rewrite 3 code samples |\n|UPDATE |`src/_documentation/_documentation/developers-and-admins/development/registration-and-authentication/external-authentication.md` |Rewrite code sample |\n|UPDATE |`src/_documentation/_documentation/developers-and-admins/development/registration-and-authentication/add-fields-to-member-objects.md` |Rewrite code sample + add note |\n\n\n### Codesamples\n\n|Action|File Path|Details|\n|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n|CREATE |`src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/MemberRoles/` |New samples: role CRUD, assignment, extending `ApplicationRole` |\n|UPDATE |`src/_code/src/Website/Program.cs` |Replace `NoOpApplicationRole` → `ApplicationRole`, `NoOpApplicationRoleStore` → `ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>`, add `RoleManager` |\n\n\n## Technical Context\n\n### Program.cs — Old Pattern (DEPRECATED)\n\n``` csharp\nbuilder.Services.AddIdentity<ApplicationUser, NoOpApplicationRole>(options =>\n{\n    // ...\n})\n    .AddUserStore<ApplicationUserStore<ApplicationUser>>()\n    .AddRoleStore<NoOpApplicationRoleStore>()\n    .AddUserManager<UserManager<ApplicationUser>>();\n```\n\n### Program.cs — New Pattern\n\n``` csharp\nbuilder.Services.AddIdentity<ApplicationUser, ApplicationRole>(options =>\n{\n    // ...\n})\n    .AddUserStore<ApplicationUserStore<ApplicationUser>>()\n    .AddRoleStore<ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>>()\n    .AddRoleManager<RoleManager<ApplicationRole>>()\n    .AddUserManager<UserManager<ApplicationUser>>();\n```\n\n### Using Statements\n\n``` csharp\nusing Kentico.Membership;             // ApplicationUser, ApplicationRole, ApplicationRoleStore, ApplicationUserStore\nusing Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity;   // RoleManager, UserManager\n```\n\n### Role CRUD (Identity Level)\n\n``` csharp\nvar roleStore = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>>();\nvar role = new ApplicationRole { Name = \"Premium\", DisplayName = \"Premium Members\", Description = \"...\" };\nawait roleStore.CreateAsync(role, cancellationToken);\nawait roleStore.UpdateAsync(role, cancellationToken);\nawait roleStore.DeleteAsync(role, cancellationToken);\nvar found = await roleStore.FindByNameAsync(\"Premium\", cancellationToken);\n```\n\n### Role CRUD (ObjectQuery Level)\n\n``` csharp\nvar provider = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<IInfoProvider<MemberRoleInfo>>();\nvar roles = provider.Get().ToList();\n```\n\n### Role Assignment\n\n``` csharp\nvar userStore = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationUserStore<ApplicationUser>>();\nawait userStore.AddToRoleAsync(user, \"Premium\", cancellationToken);\nawait userStore.RemoveFromRoleAsync(user, \"Premium\", cancellationToken);\nvar roles = await userStore.GetRolesAsync(user, cancellationToken);\nvar isInRole = await userStore.IsInRoleAsync(user, \"Premium\", cancellationToken);\n```\n\n### Extending ApplicationRole\n\n``` csharp\npublic class ExtendedApplicationRole : ApplicationRole\n{\n    public string CustomProperty { get; set; }\n    \n    public override void MapFromMemberRoleInfo(MemberRoleInfo source) { ... }\n    public override void MapToMemberRoleInfo(MemberRoleInfo target) { ... }\n}\n```\n\n### `[Authorize]` with Roles\n\n``` csharp\n// Standard ASP.NET attribute — works because ApplicationRole maps to Identity role claims\n[Authorize(Roles = \"Premium\")]\npublic IActionResult PremiumContent()\n{\n    // Only accessible to members with the \"Premium\" role\n}\n```\n\nNote: `secure-custom-endpoints.md` already documents `[Authorize]` for admin endpoints using `AdminIdentityConstants` schemes. The member roles page should note that `[Authorize(Roles = \"...\")]` works for member-facing controllers without specifying an admin scheme.\n\n### Security Pipeline Limitation\n\nNo extension points in the Xperience content access evaluation pipeline. Custom authorization logic must run at the controller/business layer AFTER content is retrieved:\n\n``` csharp\nvar article = await contentRetriever.RetrieveFirst<Article>(...);\nif (!article.HasAccess(User))\n{\n    return Forbid(); // or custom logic\n}\n```\n\n### Deprecation Info\n\n  * `NoOpApplicationRole`: `[Obsolete(\"... For real implementation use ApplicationRole instead.\"), ObsoleteSince(31, 3)]`\n  * `NoOpApplicationRoleStore`: `[Obsolete(\"... For real implementation use ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole> instead.\"), ObsoleteSince(31, 3)]`\n\n### Source File References\n\n  * `ApplicationRole`: `CMSSolution/Mvc/Kentico.Membership/Stores/Channels/ApplicationRole.cs`\n  * `ApplicationRoleStore`: `CMSSolution/Mvc/Kentico.Membership/Stores/Channels/ApplicationRoleStore.cs`\n  * `NoOpApplicationRole`: `CMSSolution/Mvc/Kentico.Membership/Stores/Channels/NoOpApplicationRole.cs`\n  * `NoOpApplicationRoleStore`: `CMSSolution/Mvc/Kentico.Membership/Stores/Channels/NoOpApplicationRoleStore.cs`\n  * `DancingGoat Program.cs`: `CMSSolution/Mvc/Projects/Kentico.Xperience.DancingGoat/Program.cs`\n  * Related existing docs: `secure-custom-endpoints.md` (Authorize attribute for admin endpoints)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Part A — New Page\n\n  * [ ] Page created at correct hierarchy location (subpage of registration-and-authentication)\n  * [ ] Role CRUD samples cover both Identity and ObjectQuery levels\n  * [ ] Role assignment/unassignment documented\n  * [ ] Custom `ApplicationRole` extension pattern documented (mirrors `ApplicationUser` pattern)\n  * [ ] `[Authorize(Roles = \"...\")]` support noted with cross-link to `secure-custom-endpoints.md`\n  * [ ] Custom authorization best practice section included (no pipeline extension points)\n  * [ ] Admin preview behavior noted briefly\n  * [ ] Cross-links to: registration-and-authentication (enablement), content retrieval (HasAccess/401/403), content sync, CI/CD reference\n\n### Part B — Auth Pages Update\n\n  * [ ] \"Does not support roles\" statement removed from registration-and-authentication.md\n  * [ ] Role enablement documented in registration-and-authentication.md (ApplicationRoleStore + RoleManager registration)\n  * [ ] All occurrences of `NoOpApplicationRole` replaced with `ApplicationRole` in code samples\n  * [ ] All occurrences of `NoOpApplicationRoleStore` replaced with `ApplicationRoleStore<ApplicationRole>`\n  * [ ] `AddRoleManager<RoleManager<ApplicationRole>>()` added where role store is registered\n  * [ ] No remaining references to NoOp types in documentation code samples\n  * [ ] Add-fields page mentions `ApplicationRole` customization pattern\n  * [ ] Codesamples `Program.cs` updated and compiles\n\n### General\n\n  * [ ] All code samples compile and reference correct namespaces\n  * [ ] Documentation builds without errors\n\n## Dependencies\n\n  * None (can be started independently)\n\n## Notes\n\n  * The `IContentItemMemberRoleRetriever` is in Internal namespace — do NOT document as public API\n  * 13 total occurrences of NoOp types across 5 existing doc files\n  * The deprecation is a **changelog-only note** — no migration guide section needed; docs simply use the new types\n  * ContentAccessSetttings will not be documented here, those are part of the next task.\n\nLabels: deprecation, documentation, member-roles, membership-roles, xperience-by-kentico\n\nPriority: Not set\n\nWas this page helpful?: Helpful\n\n⚠️ REMINDER: This task involves the code samples project (ralph-codesamples skill). The coder subagent will bootstrap the project with xpversion=https://dev.azure.com/kenticoxperience/CMS/_git/xperience/pullrequest/24883 before research begins. Build with `npm run codesamples:build` before committing any .cs files.\n⚠️ REMINDER: Admin UI interaction is enabled for this task. The coder verifies admin access; the writer can create admin objects via Playwright (see ralph-codesamples-adminui skill)."
  },
