es are truly optional, and the IA findings are properly scoped as follow-ups.\n\nI'm ready to write the analysis report now. The key takeaways are that this was executed cleanly in 66 minutes with all phases completing successfully and unanimous approval on the first pass, plus the tool selection was appropriate for the task.\n\nLooking at the rest of the findings: the parallelism worked well with all three reviewers running simultaneously, error recovery handled the tag limit gracefully with a retry, and there's a minor architectural violation where the orchestrator had to relay the scribe's outputs via MCP since the scribe lacks direct access. The proxy denials are all expected noise from standard dependencies like the .NET SDK and Chromium. The orchestrator also correctly skipped a git push and went straight to progress tracking.\n\nThe scribe received the dispatch with actual summary data and review results rather than just file references, which is an efficient data relay pattern. All eight subagents contributed manifest entries, and the orchestrator made 70 tool calls total—solid efficiency for what was accomplished. Now I'm moving on to write the final report and status.json.",
